name:Kyrie (Missa pro defunctis);
office-part:Kyriale;
mode:6;
book:Graduale Romanum, 1961, p. 94* & The Liber Usualis, 1961, p. 1807 & Chants of the Church, 1956, p. 61 & Graduale Romanum, 1974, p. 767 (XVIII B) & Vatican II Hymnal, 2011, p. 191;
transcriber:Andrew Hinkley;
% GregoBase chant 541, written out nine-fold as in the Vatican II Hymnal (GregoBase
% has iij./ij.).  Pitches identical to GregoBase 10377 (Graduale Romanum, 1974,
% "Kyrie XVIII B").  Slur groups, bars, key and text follow the melody (top line)
% of the Hymnal's organ accompaniment, p. 191; the asterisk stands before the
% second "e" of the first and last invocation, as there.  The final long G of the
% last "Ky-ri-e" melisma is slurred with the preceding C D C B-flat A in the
% Hymnal; the converter cannot slur a long note with short ones, so it stands alone.
%%
